1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,250
Did you know that octopuses
have three hearts?

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,250
Imagine that!

3
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:06,250
Let’s explore why they
need so many

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,551
Think of one heart as the
main pump

5
00:00:08,551 --> 00:00:10,470
like the big engine of a train

6
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:13,215
This heart sends blood all
around the octopus's body

7
00:00:13,215 --> 00:00:14,407
giving it the energy to

8
00:00:14,407 --> 00:00:16,408
swim and explore the ocean

9
00:00:16,408 --> 00:00:20,908
This is much like how your
heart pushes blood through
your body so you can run

10
00:00:20,908 --> 00:00:22,908
and play

11
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:26,268
But the octopus is special
because it also has two extra
hearts

12
00:00:26,268 --> 00:00:26,847
like little

13
00:00:26,847 --> 00:00:28,847
helpers

14
00:00:28,847 --> 00:00:30,763
These two hearts focus on its
gills

15
00:00:30,763 --> 00:00:32,784
which are the octopus's way
to breathe

16
00:00:32,784 --> 00:00:33,338
underwater

17
00:00:33,338 --> 00:00:35,597
just like how you breathe air
with your lungs

18
00:00:35,597 --> 00:00:38,732
The helper hearts keep the
blood moving through the
gills quickly

19
00:00:38,732 --> 00:00:39,255
making sure

20
00:00:39,255 --> 00:00:41,786
the octopus gets plenty of
oxygen from the water

21
00:00:41,786 --> 00:00:43,665
So next time you think of an
octopus

22
00:00:43,665 --> 00:00:45,444
remember those three
hearts working

23
00:00:45,444 --> 00:00:47,444
together

24
00:00:47,444 --> 00:00:48,631
It's like having a team of
little engines

25
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:49,509
each with its own important
job

